-- Plan 54 criterion 3: `:=` against a binding that is not `mut`.
--
-- The point of the fixture is what Redox does **not** do. `is_mut` is set only
-- by the literal `mut` keyword and the emitter writes `mut` only when it is
-- set, so Redox has no mechanism to make this compile and never silently adds
-- one. rustc answers `E0384`, and `redox check` maps it back onto this file —
-- which is `every check rustc can make, rustc makes` working on the one
-- construct where a compiler might be tempted to be helpful instead.
--
-- `tests/ui/` cannot hold this case: that harness runs `redox build`, which
-- never invokes rustc, so a program whose only fault is a borrow-checker
-- error builds clean there and the harness fails on its own assertion. Plan
-- 54 criterion 3 named `tests/ui/`; §11.1 is the correction.
--
-- The assignment is on line 19, column 3.
main : ()
main =
  total = 1
  total := 2
  print total
